{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 23,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.815,
            0.049,
            0.862,
            0.065
          ],
          "content": "Area"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.086,
            0.399,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": "? How many $\\mathbf { c m } ^ { 2 }$ is 10 in<sup>2</sup> ?"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.319,
            0.111,
            0.678,
            0.132
          ],
          "content": "10\\  in ^2 = 10 \\times 6.4516\\  cm ^2 = 64.516\\  cm ^2.",
          "image_source": "images/page_23_equation_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.147,
            0.404,
            0.17
          ],
          "content": "？ Convert 161.29 $\\mathbf { c m } ^ { 2 }$ to $\\operatorname { i n } ^ { 2 } ,$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.172,
            0.515,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": "Every 6.4516 $\\mathbf { c m } ^ { 2 }$ gives an $\\operatorname { i n } ^ { 2 } ,$ Hence,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.387,
            0.195,
            0.611,
            0.223
          ],
          "content": "161.29\\  cm ^2 = \\frac{161.29}{6.4516}\\  in ^2.",
          "image_source": "images/page_23_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.224,
            0.372,
            0.249
          ],
          "content": "Evaluate the quotient."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.262,
            0.803,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": "？ What do you think is the area of your classroom? Areas of classroom, house, etc., are generally measured in $\\mathrm { f t ^ { 2 } }$ or $\\mathbf { m } ^ { 2 } ,$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.316,
            0.373,
            0.34
          ],
          "content": "？ How many $\\mathrm { i n } ^ { 2 }$ is $1   \\mathrm { f t ^ { 2 } ? }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.353,
            0.845,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": "？ What do you think is the area of your school? Make an estimate and compare it with the actual data."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.396,
            0.622,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": "Larger areas of land are also measured in acres."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.408,
            0.419,
            0.592,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": "1 \\; \\mathrm { a c r e } = 4 3 , 5 \\bar { 6 } 0 \\; \\mathrm { f t } ^ { 2 } .",
          "image_source": "images/page_23_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.443,
            0.846,
            0.484
          ],
          "content": "Besides these units, different parts of India use different local units for measuring area, such as bigha, gaj, katha, dhur, cent, ankanam, etc."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.492,
            0.731,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": "？ Find out the local unit of area measurement in your region."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.528,
            0.845,
            0.592
          ],
          "content": "？ What do you think is the area of your village/town/city? Make an estimate and compare it with the actual data. Larger areas are measured in km<sup>2</sup>."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.6,
            0.392,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": "？ How many $\\mathrm { m } ^ { 2 }$ is a $\\mathrm { k m ^ { 2 } }   ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.636,
            0.801,
            0.66
          ],
          "content": "？ How many times is your village/town/city bigger than your school?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.672,
            0.772,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": "？ Find the city with the largest area in (i) India, and (ii) the world."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.708,
            0.785,
            0.732
          ],
          "content": "？ Find the city with the smallest area in (i) India, and (ii) the world."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.406,
            0.751,
            0.592,
            0.776
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "SUMMARY"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.788,
            0.568,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": "y Area of a triangl $e = { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\times$ base × height."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.813,
            0.822,
            0.851
          ],
          "content": "The area of any polygon can be evaluated by breaking it into triangles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.855,
            0.596,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": "y Area of a parallelogram = base × height."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.884,
            0.676,
            0.909
          ],
          "content": "y Area of a rhombus $= { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\times$ product of its diagonals."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.914,
            0.74,
            0.94
          ],
          "content": "y Area of a trapezium $= { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\times$ height × sum of parallel sides."
        },
